{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [36.8503, 62.77884879999999, 77.5658142, 71.21903173333328], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 79.12666530000001, 287.9304774, 99.62448646666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "This recommendation pertains to the use of primary anticoagulant prophylaxis."}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 106.50966129999995, 287.927795, 148.94687346666672], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "The panel acknowledged that there may be pediatric patients who may benefit from prophylaxis. A thorough assessment of individual risks and careful consideration of benefits and harms when considering prophylactic anticoagulation is appropriate."}, {"bbox": [36.85088, 159.94956380000008, 160.8471544, 168.38974673333337], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "Antiphospholipid antibodies"}, {"bbox": [36.8503, 175.87187259999996, 287.92728859999994, 228.14804546666664], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 4, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 7. In pediatric patients with APS, the ASH/ ISTH guideline panel suggests using secondary anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than no secondary anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁⨁ ◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [36.851212, 236.14530380000008, 77.5667262, 244.58548673333337], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 5, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 252.43666329999996, 287.927795, 283.93298846666664], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 6, "source": "docling", "text": "An a priori decision was made to exclude pediatric patients receiving only antiplatelet therapy from this evidence profile (EP)."}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 290.81767529999996, 287.94392580000005, 322.31442746666664], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 7, "source": "docling", "text": "The included evidence showed moderate benefit of secondary anticoagulation prophylaxis (with or without antiplatelet therapy) in reducing recurrent thromboembolism."}, {"bbox": [36.8503, 338.2408906, 287.93679779999997, 401.51505046666665], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 8, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 8. In pediatric patients with persistently positive antiphospholipid antibodies (APLA) without a history of thrombosis, the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests no primary anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than primary anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [36.851608, 409.5123078, 77.5671222, 417.9524907333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 9, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 425.8036673, 287.927795, 468.24188746666664], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 10, "source": "docling", "text": "An a priori decision was made to exclude pediatric patients receiving antiplatelet therapy, and therefore the panel cannot comment on the benefits and risk of using antiplatelet agents in this cohort."}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 475.12666529999996, 287.94572300000004, 550.4456224666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 11, "source": "docling", "text": "The panel acknowledges that evolving definitions of APS may influence clinical decision-making and emphasizes that individual patient characteristics, such as the presence of an underlying autoimmune disorder, double or triple antibody positivity, the strength of antibody titers, and microvascular manifestations, should be considered when evaluating the need for primary anticoagulant prophylaxis."}, {"bbox": [36.85088, 563.4325508, 209.3211108, 571.8727337333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 12, "source": "docling", "text": "Patients who have experienced trauma"}, {"bbox": [36.8503, 579.3558966, 287.9390056, 631.6312304666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 13, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 9. In pediatric patients who have experienced trauma, the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests no anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [36.850979, 639.6283058, 77.56649320000002, 648.0684887333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 14, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [36.963703, 655.9206643, 287.9304774, 698.4148914666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 15, "source": "docling", "text": "The evidence does not support the universal use of anticoagulant prophylaxis in pediatric trauma patients who compose a heterogenous population in whom the overall prevalence of VTE is low."}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 61.665667299999996, 556.9298984000001, 126.04318746666672], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 16, "source": "docling", "text": "There are, however, subgroups in the included studies (patients deemed at 'high risk') that had higher reported rates of VTE who may benefit from prophylactic anticoagulation. These specific high-risk criteria included presence of shock, age of >12 years (or younger ages with multiple risk factors), immobility, intubation, and presence of a CVAD."}, {"bbox": [305.858368, 134.9952856, 556.9083688000001, 165.38773046666665], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 17, "source": "docling", "text": "Although the risk for bleeding from anticoagulant prophylaxis in pediatric trauma patients is overall low, it was noted to be higher in patients receiving prophylactic anticoagulation in 1 study."}, {"bbox": [305.858368, 176.39048179999998, 399.41707979999995, 184.83066473333326], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 18, "source": "docling", "text": "Hospitalized patients"}, {"bbox": [305.857971, 192.31285160000004, 556.927415, 233.64700846666665], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 19, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 10. In hospitalized pediatric patients, the ASH/ ISTH guideline panel suggests no anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁⨁ ◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [305.860596, 241.64426579999997, 346.57611019999996, 250.08444873333326], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 20, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 257.93568629999993, 556.9200562, 289.43246946666665], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 21, "source": "docling", "text": "Hospitalized pediatric patients encompass an extremely heterogeneous population with respect to age, underlying medical conditions, and baseline risk of thrombosis."}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 296.3166683, 556.8985284, 338.7548874666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 22, "source": "docling", "text": "The panel acknowledged that there may be certain pediatric patients that may benefit from anticoagulant prophylaxis (eg, immobility, use of estrogen, infection, obesity, inflammation), although additional studies are needed."}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 345.5836663, 556.8904758000001, 366.13849346666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 23, "source": "docling", "text": "Several subgroups (cancer, CVAD, surgery, and trauma) are addressed in separate recommendations."}, {"bbox": [305.858368, 379.12452079999997, 427.7484885999999, 387.5647037333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 24, "source": "docling", "text": "Patients with critical illness"}, {"bbox": [305.857971, 395.0468906, 556.9361996, 447.32300346666665], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 25, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 11. In pediatric patients who are critically ill with or without a CVAD, the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests no anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [305.859314, 455.32026079999997, 346.57482819999996, 463.7604437333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 26, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 471.6116513, 556.9245305999999, 514.1059004666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 27, "source": "docling", "text": "The current evidence does not support the universal use of prophylactic anticoagulation in critically ill children for which there are insufficient data for formal stratification of the risks of VTE and the risk of bleeding."}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 520.9346643, 556.9225194959997, 574.3712204666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 28, "source": "docling", "text": "However, the panel acknowledged that there may be subgroups of children who are critically ill (children aged ≥ 1 year with an untunneled CVAD and low risk of bleeding and children receiving IMV), for whom the risk of VTE may outweigh the risk of bleeding, who could potentially benefit from prophylactic anticoagulation."}, {"bbox": [305.858368, 586.3369238, 431.1457793999999, 594.7771067333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 29, "source": "docling", "text": "Patients undergoing surgery"}, {"bbox": [305.857971, 602.2598876, 556.9363400000001, 654.5352224666667], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 30, "source": "docling", "text": "RECOMMENDATION 12. In children undergoing noncardiac surgery, the ASH/ISTH guideline panel suggests no anticoagulant prophylaxis rather than anticoagulant prophylaxis (conditional recommendation based on very low certainty in the evidence about effects ⨁ ◯◯◯ )."}, {"bbox": [305.859375, 662.5322898, 346.5748892, 670.9724727333333], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 31, "source": "docling", "text": "Remarks:"}, {"bbox": [305.972015, 678.8809533, 556.9074986, 699.3790944666666], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 5, "seq": 32, "source": "docling", "text": "The panel did not assess VTE risk by specific type of surgical procedure (eg, orthopedic, bariatric, laparoscopic, etc). Rather,"}], "checksum": "31d2a4d8474aa1ce23d0784057336e4aadc74be03afc444b5414546251201949", "content_present": true, "doc_id": "d-97b717427b6bf503", "docling_version": "2.118.0", "engine_version": "2.118.0", "errors": [], "images": [], "page_index": 4, "page_sizes": {"5": [593.9719848632812, 782.9860229492188]}, "route": "docling", "schema_version": "v0.1.0", "source_hash": "97b717427b6bf503d2817d27c02c788bde996058c4ef8ebaee3678ae31782ea1", "status": "ok", "tables": [], "timings": {}}